Dodam's one change to Harbor 0.25.0: harbor/environments/docker/docker.py

Harbor starts every command in a task container with `docker compose exec -e NAME=VALUE ...`.
The values of the agent's environment, the subscription token among them, then sit in the
command line of host processes, which any process of the same user can read.

With this change Harbor passes three names, and only these, by name (`-e NAME`):
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN, the names the pilot and
Harbor's Claude Code agent pass credentials under. Their values reach the docker CLI through
that process's environment, from which docker compose reads them. Every other variable is
passed exactly as the released Harbor passes it, on the command line, and nothing else of the
agent's environment enters the host docker CLI's own environment. So a secret under any other
name (a proxy address with a password in it, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS, another agent's API
key) is still on the command line: this change covers the listed names only, and the pilot
refuses to pass its token under any other. Other container runtimes, such as Podman, are left
as they were.

Apply it from bench/ with `python -m dodambench.harbor_patch apply`. The pilot refuses to hand
the token to a Harbor that is not 0.25.0 with exactly this change.

